<title>MEXICO: FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 22.66 pct.</title>
<headline>FORECAST-Mexico 28-day Cetes seen up to 22.66 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Interest rates on Mexico's bellwether 28-day Cetes, or T-bills, are seen rising 80 basis points to 22.66 percent, and rates are also seen rising at longer terms, according to a Reuters' survey of nine Cetes dealers.</p>
<p>Following is a table comparing last week's primary rates versus expectations for this week's auction and the expected change in basis points.</p>
<p>    TERM	LAST WEEK    THIS WEEK'S SURVEY	CHANGE</p>
<p>    28-DAY     21.86	    22.66		     80 bps</p>
<p>    91-DAY     21.90	    22.77		     87 bps</p>
<p>    182-DAY    22.40	    23.17		     77 bps</p>
<p>    1-YEAR     23.90	    23.99			9 bps</p>
<p>The results will be released by Banco de Mexico at 1830 (2330 GMT)</p>
<p>((- Mexico City newsroom 525 7289559))</p>
</text>
